  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study Climate Smart Agriculture (CSA) Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate change causes environmental problems and affects the development of the agricultural sector in Kenya. There is an urgent need to implement climate-smart solutions to help farmers adapt to a changing climate. The Netherlands can play an essential role in designing CSA plans for Kenya. The Netherlands, as an expert in the field of Smart Agriculture, can help in finding solutions for the growing climatic issues in Kenya. On the one hand, there is a need within the Kenyan agricultural sector to use climate-smart techniques to enhance climate resilience and food security and safety. On the other hand, there is a growing amount of techniques and knowledge available in the Netherlands which can provide solutions for this increasing climatic problem in Kenya. The Netherlands Embassy has proposed conducting a market study to connect the demand and supply sides. This study will investigate the business opportunities for Dutch initiatives and innovations focused on smart agriculture techniques in Kenya. It will also explore the current needs and demands of the Kenyan agricultural sector to adapt to climate change sustainably.</narrative>
  </description>
